       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults.\n\n- **Per dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual single-dose maximum of 800 mg.\n- **Per day:** 6,400 mg/day is double the maximum of 3,200 mg/day. Even 3,200 mg/day is normally used only under close supervision, such as for inflammatory arthritis.\n- **Risks:** The main risks are GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't make this dose safe.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or **800 mg four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the intended dose and frequency, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, I can't enter it as written. Please confirm it with pharmacy or the attending first."
